    <string name="time_story_park_duration">3.13 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_park">In 2023, Max Park solved a 3×3 Rubik’s Cube in 3.13 seconds.</string>
    <string name="time_story_wright_first_duration">12 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_wright_first">In 1903, the Wright brothers’ first powered flight covered about 36 metres in 12 seconds.</string>
    <string name="time_story_wright_fourth_duration">59 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_wright_fourth">On the day of their first successful powered flight, the Wright brothers’ fourth flight lasted 59 seconds.</string>
    <string name="time_story_bannister_duration">3 minutes 59.4 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_bannister">In 1954, Roger Bannister ran a mile in 3 minutes 59.4 seconds, becoming the first person to break the four-minute barrier.</string>
    <string name="time_story_cage_duration">4 minutes 33 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_cage">At the 1952 premiere of John Cage’s 4′33″, the pianist never pressed a key. Wind, rain and sounds from the audience filled the piece instead.</string>
    <string name="time_story_balloon_duration">8 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_balloon">In 1783, a sheep, a duck and a rooster flew together in a hot-air balloon for eight minutes. All three returned alive and were given a home in the royal menagerie at Versailles.</string>
    <string name="time_story_shepard_duration">15 minutes 22 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_shepard">In 1961, Alan Shepard’s first spaceflight took 15 minutes 22 seconds from launch to splashdown.</string>
    <string name="time_story_queen_duration">About 21 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_queen">Queen’s set at Wembley for Live Aid in 1985 lasted about 21 minutes. That is the length of a performance still remembered today.</string>
    <string name="time_story_white_duration">About 23 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_white">In 1965, Ed White began his spacewalk above the Pacific near Hawaii. About 23 minutes later, it ended above the Gulf of Mexico.</string>
    <string name="time_story_ganna_duration">1 hour</string>
    <string name="time_story_ganna">In 2022, Filippo Ganna cycled 56.792 kilometres on an indoor track in a single hour.</string>
    <string name="time_story_gagarin_duration">1 hour 48 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_gagarin">In 1961, Yuri Gagarin’s journey as the first human in space lasted 108 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_honnold_duration">3 hours 56 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_honnold">In 2017, Alex Honnold climbed El Capitan without a safety rope. The ascent took 3 hours and 56 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_tennis_duration">11 hours 5 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_tennis">At Wimbledon in 2010, Isner and Mahut played one match across three days. Playing time alone added up to 11 hours 5 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_beatles_duration">1 day</string>
    <string name="time_story_beatles">On 11 February 1963, the Beatles recorded ten of the fourteen tracks for their debut album, Please Please Me, in one day.</string>
    <string name="time_story_lindbergh_duration">33 hours 30 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_lindbergh">In 1927, Charles Lindbergh flew alone and nonstop from New York to Paris. Crossing the Atlantic took 33 hours 30 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_rocky_duration">3½ days</string>
    <string name="time_story_rocky">After months of thinking it over, Sylvester Stallone wrote the first rough draft of Rocky in three and a half days. Two further drafts followed.</string>
    <string name="time_story_mozart_duration">About 4 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_mozart">In 1783, Mozart had a concert approaching but no symphony with him. He wrote a new one, the Linz Symphony, in about four days.</string>
    <string name="time_story_gemini_duration">About 4 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_gemini">In 1965, the two astronauts aboard Gemini IV spent about four days in Earth orbit.</string>
    <string name="time_story_apollo_duration">About 8 days 3 hours</string>
    <string name="time_story_apollo">In 1969, Apollo 11 took about eight days and three hours to launch, land on the Moon and return to Earth.</string>
    <string name="time_story_handel_duration">24 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_handel">In 1741, Handel completed the first score of Messiah in 24 days. He later revised it for performances.</string>
    <string name="time_story_picasso_duration">About 5 weeks</string>
    <string name="time_story_picasso">Guernica is about 7.8 metres wide. In 1937, Picasso took about five weeks to bring it from the first sketches to the finished painting.</string>
    <string name="time_story_dickens_duration">About 6 weeks</string>
    <string name="time_story_dickens">In 1843, Charles Dickens wrote A Christmas Carol in about six weeks.</string>
    <string name="time_story_bly_duration">About 72 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_bly">Inspired by Around the World in Eighty Days, journalist Nellie Bly set out on a real journey around the globe. It took about 72 days.</string>
    <string name="time_story_minecraft_duration">About 3 months</string>
    <string name="time_story_minecraft">The early mobile version of Minecraft was put together in about three months. Multiplayer was not even part of the original plan.</string>
    <string name="time_story_perseverance_duration">203 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_perseverance">In 2021, the Perseverance rover landed on Mars after a 203-day journey from Earth.</string>
    <string name="time_story_empire_duration">1 year 45 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_empire">New York’s 102-story Empire State Building was built in one year and 45 days. Construction began in 1930 and finished the following year.</string>
